    "facts": [
      "A pointer local without an initializer lowers to the generic typed Inst::Uninitialized form rendered as uninitialized.ptr or uninitialized.fnptr.",
      "The validator and Section 9 reader already treated pointer poison as ordinary non-effect data; object and function pointer forms round-trip byte-identically.",
      "Pointer poison may cross a CFG edge or be overwritten without a semantic read.",
      "Dereferencing an uninitialized object pointer and calling an uninitialized function pointer report E3013 in both interpreters.",
      "A pointer-to-integer or non-null integer-to-pointer conversion reports E3036; a null pointer constant still lowers."
    ],
    "egraphBoundary": "Both eligibility implementations exclude Inst::Uninitialized as a family; no pointer or function-pointer poison enters the scalar e-graph."
  },
